# TRIPBOX_BASE_URL=https://flights.example.com/tripbox
# Caddy in front of AirTrail and tripbox at one hostname: tripbox under /tripbox, AirTrail at the
# root. AirTrail must be at the root (it is served under no path of its own), and its ORIGIN
# setting is this hostname, https://flights.example.com. Caddy gets and renews the certificate by
# itself. "web:8110" is tripbox's page and "airtrail:3000" is AirTrail when Caddy is a service in
# the same compose project as both; for a Caddy on the host, write their published addresses.
# tripbox's worker reaches AirTrail directly, not through this proxy:
# TRIPBOX_AIRTRAIL_URL=http://airtrail:3000. The address people open AirTrail at,
# TRIPBOX_AIRTRAIL_PUBLIC_URL, is the hostname: https://flights.example.com. AirTrail's Trips button
# is built with /tripbox (integrations/airtrail/build.sh).
# The path is handed on as it came (no handle_path, no strip_prefix): tripbox answers under it.
# AirTrail answers everything else, in the last handle; a path such as /tripboxx is AirTrail's.
flights.example.com {
	@tripbox path /tripbox /tripbox/*
	handle @tripbox {
		reverse_proxy web:8110
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy airtrail:3000
	}
}
